{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ef1a0c99-5026-42d3-a433-aa775cb0a573","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-91b74ca8ea452413","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-atsnhp6_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Link registered model versions to source runs and open comparison from the Model Registry\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: registered model versions\nrecord a link back to the run that produced them, and a user browsing the\nregistry can open a run comparison starting from a registered model version.\nThis lets model promotion decisions start from the registry — the catalog of\nrecord for candidate models — instead of requiring users to hunt for the\noriginating runs manually.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Record, on each registered model version, the link to the run that produced\n  it (the mechanism — e.g. an existing metadata/extension point on model\n  versions — is an implementation decision for the Model Registry team).\n- Surface the source-run link in the Model Registry user experience.\n- Provide an entry point from a registered model version (and/or its linked\n  run) that opens the Dashboard run comparison for the linked run.\n- Capture the run identity at registration time or via backfill for model\n  versions registered while the lineage capability is being introduced, as the\n  team's implementation design determines.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version was registered from a run, when a user views that\n  model version in the Model Registry, then the version shows the link back to\n  the run that produced it.\n- Given a model version with a linked run, when the user opens the comparison\n  entry point, then the Dashboard run comparison opens for the linked run\n  (verified against the Dashboard comparison capability; the entry point\n  targets the comparison view via a link, so this epic proceeds in parallel\n  with the Dashboard-side work and this criterion gates on the linked view\n  resolving correctly).\n- The midstream build pipeline for the Model Registry repository is green\n  with these changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n  them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — covered by the\n  lineage link and the comparison entry point.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27935,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0bd049c0bb08c54","agent_id":"a5811cc96de0ed59b","session_id":"e15f0d7e-da02-4fea-9fcd-2440258fc805","uuid":"30767a5e-95de-4e71-b0d6-a9de450f113a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:17:31.171Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
