{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88fbbf8a6a71fed5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9015\n11\t\n12\tExperiment comparison for training and pipeline runs.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below threshold: the strategy spans three affected components (Dashboard,\n17\tModel Registry, Data Science Pipelines) and multiple distinct work streams\n18\t(Dashboard UI feature, Model Registry integration, substantive documentation\n19\tauthoring). Not documentation-only: active code components are present.\n20\t\n21\t## Epic List\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n24\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 | Run comparison view with side-by-side and diff modes in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 | Link registered model versions to source runs and open comparison from the Model Registry | Implementation | Model Registry | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 | Document the run comparison workflow from the runs list and the Model Registry | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n28\t\n29\t## Component Graph\n30\t\n31\t| Component | Classification | Rationale |\n32\t|-----------|----------------|-----------|\n33\t| Dashboard | Active | New comparison UI (side-by-side and diff modes) — code changes in the odh-dashboard console. Corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` (user-facing enablement of any component requires a Dashboard integration; pipeline runs are surfaced in the Dashboard). |\n34\t| Model Registry | Active | Model versions must link back to the run that produced them and expose an entry point to open a comparison. Corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/model-registry.md` (training lineage is part of the registry's role; custom properties on model versions are the extension point for structured metadata). |\n35\t| Data Science Pipelines | Passive | No code change stated in the strategy: pipeline run parameters and metrics already surface on per-run pages in the Dashboard, so the comparison feature reads existing metadata. Validation (comparison works for pipeline runs as well as training runs) is an acceptance criterion on the Dashboard comparison epic (E001), owned by the same delivery surface; the RHOAI Pipelines team owns no epic. Corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md` (KFP v2 runs surfaced in the Dashboard). |\n36\t\n37\tAll three components exist in architecture context and are already Konflux\n38\tonboarded — no onboarding chains or new-component provisioning needed.\n39\t\n40\t## Dependency DAG\n41\t\n42\t```mermaid\n43\tgraph TD\n44\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9015-E001 Dashboard comparison view]\n45\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9015-E002 Registry run link-back]\n46\t    E003[RHAISTRAT-9015-E003 Comparison docs]\n47\t    E001 --> E003\n48\t    E002 --> E003\n49\t```\n50\t\n51\t## DAG Justification\n52\t\n53\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n54\t|------|------|-----------|\n55\t| (none) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 15 (parallel) | Different components, different teams, different repos (odh-dashboard vs model-registry). No shared build artifact: the Dashboard comparison does not build against a Model Registry API, and the registry's \"open a comparison\" entry point targets the comparison view via a link (a configuration reference / URL), not an API or CRD it compiles against. Per Rule 13, configuration references are AC gates, not DAG edges — the registry epic carries an acceptance criterion that its entry point opens the Dashboard run comparison for the linked runs. |\n56\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation describes the comparison workflow as built, including the Dashboard-side view. |\n57\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Documentation covers the registry-originated comparison path, which depends on the link-back existing. |\n58\t\n59\tNo Investigation epics: the strategy's Open Questions section is \"None\", and\n60\tthere are no risks, assumptions, pending reviews, or conditional ADRs. All\n61\tremaining unknowns (e.g. which metadata field carries the run link on a model\n62\tversion, how the comparison view is addressed for deep-linking) are\n63\timplementation details the owning teams resolve — captured as acceptance\n64\tcriteria, not investigations.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n67\t\n68\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n69\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n70\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | Side-by-side comparison of parameters and metrics for two or more selected runs in the Dashboard. |\n71\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E002 | Registered model versions link back to the producing run; comparison can be opened from the Model Registry. |\n72\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (bundled) | The diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface over the same run parameters and metrics as HLR-1 — same component (Dashboard), same team, same data. The strategy itself notes the requirements were consolidated from two customer councils with overlapping wording kept. Splitting would build the same UI surface twice and add an artificial serialization edge between two epics rendering the same run data; the diff highlighting is not independently deferrable from the side-by-side view it renders on top of. Bundled at the higher priority (P0). |\n73\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E003 | Documentation of the comparison workflow from both entry points (runs list and registry). Substantive new doc topics → separate docs-authoring epic per work-product type boundary. |\n74\t\n75\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n76\t\n77\t## Health Warnings\n78\t\n79\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n80\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n81\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Owner teams were inferred from the architecture\n82\t  context files (RHOAI Dashboard, Model Registry, RHOAI Pipelines); epic\n83\t  acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs. The docs epic's owner\n84\t  (RHOAI Dashboard) is an inference — confirm with the Documentation component\n85\t  owners.\n86\t- **HLR overlap**: HLR-1 (P0) and HLR-3 (P1) describe the same comparison\n87\t  surface in different words (flagged in the strategy's problem statement as\n88\t  consolidated from two customer councils). Consolidated into one epic per the\n89\t  redundant-HLR rule rather than split by priority — see the traceability\n90\t  matrix row for HLR-3.\n91\t- **Passive component**: Data Science Pipelines requires no code change; its\n92\t  validation is an acceptance criterion on the Dashboard comparison epic. If\n93\t  pipeline run metadata proves insufficient for comparison during\n94\t  implementation, that is a fix-and-retry on the Dashboard epic, not a new\n95\t  epic (no genuine unknown was flagged by the strategy).\n96\t- No priority inversions detected. No scope traps detected (out-of-scope items\n97\t  — automatic best-run selection, cross-cluster/cross-project comparison — are\n98\t  respected and do not contradict any epic scope).\n99\t\n100\t## Tiered Delivery\n101\t\n102\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7c195cc3f4fe6b8","agent_id":"a6354f177820eac5e","session_id":"e15f0d7e-da02-4fea-9fcd-2440258fc805","uuid":"08d7cf83-642a-4f98-95fb-3bbe355f2b24","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:19:29.121Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88fbbf8a6a71fed5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_d