{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eca0c0f03082268","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E001\n3\ttitle: Run comparison view with side-by-side and diff modes in the Dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Run comparison view with side-by-side and diff modes in the Dashboard\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a run comparison capability in the Dashboard: users select\n34\ttwo or more training or pipeline runs and view their parameters and metrics\n35\tside by side, with a diff presentation that highlights which parameters and\n36\tmetrics changed between two selected runs. This gives data scientists\n37\tin-platform visibility into what changed between candidate runs, replacing the\n38\tcurrent exported-spreadsheet workflow that model promotion decisions depend on.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Add multi-run selection from the existing runs list (two or more runs).\n43\t- Render a comparison view showing the parameters and metrics of every\n44\t  selected run side by side.\n45\t- Provide a diff presentation of the comparison that highlights which\n46\t  parameters and metrics changed between two selected runs (values that\n47\t  differ between the two runs are visually distinguished from identical\n48\t  values).\n49\t- Read run parameters and metrics from the same per-run metadata already\n50\t  surfaced on run detail pages, covering both training runs and Data Science\n51\t  Pipelines runs.\n52\t- Comparison operates within the project the runs belong to; cross-project and\n53\t  cross-cluster comparison is out of scope per the strategy.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- Given a user has selected two or more runs in the runs list, when they open\n58\t  the comparison, then the parameters and metrics of all selected runs are\n59\t  displayed side by side.\n60\t- Given two runs are selected for comparison, when the diff presentation is\n61\t  shown, then the parameters and metrics that changed between the two runs are\n62\t  highlighted and distinguishable from unchanged values.\n63\t- Given runs of both kinds are selected (training runs and Data Science\n64\t  Pipelines runs), when the comparison is opened, then parameters and metrics\n65\t  for both kinds of runs are displayed (validates that the passive Data\n66\t  Science Pipelines component keeps working with no code change on its side).\n67\t- The comparison view is reachable from the runs list without leaving the\n68\t  project scope of the selected runs.\n69\t- The midstream build pipeline for the Dashboard repository is green with\n70\t  these changes.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: Users can select two or more runs and view their parameters\n75\t  and metrics side by side in the Dashboard — covered by the multi-run\n76\t  selection and side-by-side comparison view.\n77\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: Provide a run \"diff\" view that highlights which parameters\n78\t  and metrics changed between two selected runs — covered by the diff\n79\t  presentation of the same comparison surface. Bundled with HLR-1 rather than\n80\t  split: the diff view is a presentation mode of the same comparison surface\n81\t  over the same run parameters and metrics (same component, same team), and\n82\t  the strategy notes these requirements were consolidated from two customer\n83\t  councils with overlapping wording; splitting would build the same UI surface\n84\t  twice and is not independently deferrable.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7c195cc3f4fe6b8","agent_id":"a6354f177820eac5e","session_id":"e15f0d7e-da02-4fea-9fcd-2440258fc805","uuid":"df12ff3b-d8c6-4ae6-97c5-ab4773875912","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:19:31.907Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8eca0c0f03082268","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
