{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-841db200ae9e83ac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9015-E002\n3\ttitle: Link registered model versions to source runs and open comparison from the\n4\t  Model Registry\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9015\n6\tcomponent: Model Registry\n7\tteam: Model Registry\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Link registered model versions to source runs and open comparison from the Model Registry\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic delivers run lineage in the Model Registry: registered model versions\n35\trecord a link back to the run that produced them, and a user browsing the\n36\tregistry can open a run comparison starting from a registered model version.\n37\tThis lets model promotion decisions start from the registry — the catalog of\n38\trecord for candidate models — instead of requiring users to hunt for the\n39\toriginating runs manually.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Record, on each registered model version, the link to the run that produced\n44\t  it (the mechanism — e.g. an existing metadata/extension point on model\n45\t  versions — is an implementation decision for the Model Registry team).\n46\t- Surface the source-run link in the Model Registry user experience.\n47\t- Provide an entry point from a registered model version (and/or its linked\n48\t  run) that opens the Dashboard run comparison for the linked run.\n49\t- Capture the run identity at registration time or via backfill for model\n50\t  versions registered while the lineage capability is being introduced, as the\n51\t  team's implementation design determines.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a model version was registered from a run, when a user views that\n56\t  model version in the Model Registry, then the version shows the link back to\n57\t  the run that produced it.\n58\t- Given a model version with a linked run, when the user opens the comparison\n59\t  entry point, then the Dashboard run comparison opens for the linked run\n60\t  (verified against the Dashboard comparison capability; the entry point\n61\t  targets the comparison view via a link, so this epic proceeds in parallel\n62\t  with the Dashboard-side work and this criterion gates on the linked view\n63\t  resolving correctly).\n64\t- The midstream build pipeline for the Model Registry repository is green\n65\t  with these changes.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Registered model versions link back to the run that produced\n70\t  them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — covered by the\n71\t  lineage link and the comparison entry point.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7c195cc3f4fe6b8","agent_id":"a6354f177820eac5e","session_id":"e15f0d7e-da02-4fea-9fcd-2440258fc805","uuid":"03ffb2c6-81af-4929-aece-eab28d962844","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:19:32.680Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-841db200ae9e83ac","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
