ent. `architecture_claims` calibration holds: E001 and E002 score 1 with rationales citing the actual architecture-context files (dashboard.md, model-registry.md) that corroborate the premises shaping them; E003 scores 0 with the correct rationale that no architecture-context file exists for the Documentation component. The E001 rationale's \"0 → 1\" notation for external_dependency is slightly odd phrasing but the frontmatter value (1, no external dependency) is consistent with the strategy. Computed scores (7, 7, 6) are pipeline-derived and not re-checked per instructions.\n34\t\n35\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n36\tEvery epic has testable Given/When/Then or verifiable ACs derived from the HLRs. The docs-authoring epic (E003) carries the rule-mandated technical-review AC. There is no replacement of existing behavior (new capability), so no rollback/feature-flag AC is required; no konflux chain exists here, though E001 and E002 both still carry build-pipeline-green ACs. E002's entry-point AC gates on the Dashboard comparison view resolving — a condition on the epic's own deliverable gated via AC (the Rule 13-compliant shape), not an externally controlled precondition, so it is not a misfiled soft-AC. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n37\t\n38\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n39\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: HLR-1 through HLR-4 map to epics; the three affected components are dispositioned (Dashboard active in E001, Model Registry active in E002, Data Science Pipelines explicitly passive with its validation carried as an AC on E001 and the reasoning recorded in Health Warnings). Out-of-scope items (auto best-run selection, cross-cluster/cross-project comparison) are respected — E001's scope explicitly excludes cross-project/cross-cluster. The strategy's meta-context (consolidated customer councils, missing Impacted Teams / AC / NFR sections) is carried forward into the summary's Health Warnings rather than silently dropped. No conditional branches are needed (no bounded outcomes stated). HLR-4's documentation requirement is satisfied by the docs-authoring epic E003.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89070f07b0006f88","agent_id":"afb358c8a3f02ace6","session_id":"e15f0d7e-da02-4fea-9fcd-2440258fc805","uuid":"02d9ba34-cc06-49f5-ba6c-250858c9d2ca","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:21:33.521Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ca8208d6632aaa7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
